WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.590
Stage left: an old king, three daughters,

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.800
and a map of Britain, torn into pieces.

3
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:11.040
Stage right: an old earl,
two sons, and a letter,

4
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.290
forged in one son's name.

5
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.270
Each side drives a loyal child away.

6
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.760
Storm on the left.

7
00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.460
Darkness on the right.

8
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:22.700
Why would one play tell
the same story twice?

9
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.510
In this mission, you'll
walk through the five acts,

10
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.060
from the love test to the final battle.

11
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:31.050
You'll line the two
fathers up: who misjudges,

12
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.550
who suffers, who cares for them.

13
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.230
And you'll hear Gloucester
blame the heavens:

14
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.650
"These late eclipses in the sun
and moon portend no good to us".

15
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:44.820
Your mission: explain why the
play tells the same story twice.
